timestamp=2026-11-09T08:08:39.169Z level=INFO run=5a234059 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Try to understand each anomaly type\n# 1. \"One problematic station broadly follows local patterns, but not with the same rhythm as its peers.\"\n# This sounds like phase shift / lagged correlation different from others, or poor time alignment of response.\n# Or maybe correlation is lower at lag 0 but higher at lag ±k compared to nearby stations.\n# Also \"broadly follows local patterns\" - so overall shape similar, just shifted in time.\n\n# 2. \"Another looks plausible point-by-point yet its swings are unusually muted compared with comparable local stations.\"\n# Lower variance/amplitude. Maybe sensor damping? Or calibration issue flattening peaks/troughs.\n\n# 3. \"A third appears ordinary in aggregate, but its remaining deviations line up a bit too neatly with one environmental driver.\"\n# Aggregate stats might look fine. After controlling for common signal or background, residuals correlate strongly with specific weather variable.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
