timestamp=2026-11-09T08:11:03.342Z level=INFO run=5a234059 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# ST002 has a NaN at first timestamp - but peers have values. Also the pattern: \n# at 2026-01-01 20:00:00, t and ref are both ~23.77 (very close). \n# at 2026-01-02 20:00:00, t=23.25, ref=23.49 (close). \n# But other times look different - e.g. 2026-01-02 08:00:00 t=25.27, ref=15.84 (big difference). \n# Also \"broadly follows local patterns, but not with the same rhythm as its peers.\"\n# Maybe the \"rhythm\" means timing is off - time shift. But lag correlation is weak overall?\n# Or maybe it's following a different phase - like it's out of sync by some fixed offset? Or inconsistent?\n# Another interpretation: diurnal cycle is present but peaks occur at different hours. \n# Check cross-correlation with individual peers too.\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.stats as stats\n\nstations = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/stations.csv')\nreadings = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/readings.csv')\npm25 = readings[readings['pollutant']=='PM25']\npm25_pivot = pm25.pivot_table(index='timestamp', columns='station_id', values='current_reading').sort_index()\nst_info = stations.set_index('station_id')\n\ntarget = 'ST002'\nd = st_info.loc[target, 'district']\npeers = st_info[st_info['district']==d].index.intersection(pm25_pivot.columns)\npeers_ref = [p for p in peers if p != target]\n# check best lag per peer\nfor pr in peers_ref[:4]:\n    t = pm25_pivot[target].interpolate(limit=2)\n    r = pm25_pivot[pr].interpolate(limit=2)\n    best = (0, -10)\n    for lag in range(-2, 3):\n        if lag < 0:\n            a = t.iloc[:lag]; b = r.iloc[-lag:]\n        elif lag == 0:\n            a = t; b = r\n        else:\n            a = t.iloc[lag:]; b = r.iloc[:-lag]\n        try:\n            corr = stats.pearsonr(a,b)[0]\n            if corr > best[1]: best = (lag, corr)\n        except:\n            pass\n    print(f'{target} vs {pr}: lag={best[0]}, r={best[1]:.3f}')\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
