timestamp=2026-11-09T08:12:23.011Z level=INFO run=5a234059 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# So lag0 correlation is decent (0.536) when computed on valid pairs only. That means it does follow local patterns in shape.\n# But \"not with the same rhythm as its peers.\" That phrase is a bit ambiguous. Maybe it's a timing drift? Or maybe irregular sampling rhythm?\n# Also check if the missingness pattern itself is odd? \"Some measurement rows are incomplete, so treat short gaps carefully and prefer methods that preserve local time-series structure rather than turning missingness itself into the main signal.\"\n# ST002 has exactly 1 NaN at the very first timestamp (00:00:00) while most others have data there? Let us look.\nimport pandas as pd\n\nstations = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/stations.csv')\nreadings = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/readings.csv')\npm25 = readings[readings['pollutant']=='PM25']\npm25_pivot = pm25.pivot_table(index='timestamp', columns='station_id', values='current_reading').sort_index()\n\n# check first row NaNs\nfirst_row_na = pm25_pivot.iloc[0].isna().sum()\nprint('first row NaNs:', first_row_na)\nprint(pm25_pivot.iloc[0][pm25_pivot.iloc[0].isna()].head())\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
