timestamp=2026-11-09T08:13:18.204Z level=INFO run=5a234059 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# For ST002, correlation is similar across lags (around 0.54). No clear phase shift advantage. So ST002’s “rhythm” issue is less obvious from lag analysis. But earlier we saw some peers preferred lag +1 vs ST002? And also the description says \"not with the same rhythm as its peers\" — maybe it has irregular rhythm / inconsistent timing. Or perhaps it’s the “another looks plausible point-by-point yet its swings are unusually muted” — wait look up the exact text again.\n# The three: \n# 1. \"One problematic station broadly follows local patterns, but not with the same rhythm as its peers.\" \n# 2. \"Another looks plausible point-by-point yet its swings are unusually muted compared with comparable local stations.\"\n# 3. \"A third appears ordinary in aggregate, but its remaining deviations line up a bit too neatly with one environmental driver.\"\n# \n# ST066 had very muted swings, lowest variance among peers. That fits #2 perfectly.\n# ST060 had phase shift (much better correlation at different lags) — fits #1 (not with the same rhythm).\n# ST002 has one NaN at start and some oddities. Is it #1 or something else? Or maybe not one of the three?\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
