timestamp=2026-11-09T08:15:16.169Z level=INFO run=5a234059 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# ST040 values are extremely high (200+). That’s clearly problematic - possibly a calibration/unit issue or sensor malfunction.\n# Is this one of the three faulty stations? Let us check the other candidates for the specific anomaly types.\n# Anomaly 2 was \"looks plausible point-by-point yet its swings are unusually muted compared with comparable local stations\" — that’s ST066 (low variance). \n# Anomaly 1 \"broadly follows local patterns, but not with the same rhythm as its peers\" — that could be ST060 (phase shifted). Also ST040 is extreme, not following patterns at all. That’s more like an outlier/instrument failure. \n# Anomaly 3 \"appears ordinary in aggregate, but its remaining deviations line up a bit too neatly with one environmental driver\" — needs to look “ordinary in aggregate” but have residuals strongly correlated with some weather driver.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
