timestamp=2026-11-09T08:15:54.773Z level=INFO run=5a234059 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Let us summarize all three anomaly types with strongest candidates:\n# Type 1 (same rhythm issue / phase shift): ST060 (PM10, phase-shifted, lag correlations much better at non-zero lags). Also has timing/rhythm issue. This fits.\n# Type 2 (muted swings): ST066 (PM25), lowest variance among peers, muted amplitude, follows shape but dampened. Very clear fit.\n# Type 3 (deviations line up with one environmental driver, ordinary in aggregate): ST023 (PM25), aggregate stats very close to peers, but residuals strongly correlated with rain. Strongest rain-residual correlation. Also ST057 similar but lower magnitude.\n# Another possibility for type 3: ST036/ST039 have strong wind-residual correlation. But ST023’s rain correlation is very prominent.\n# Are there any other stations for type 1? ST040 is extreme outlier (not just rhythm) — probably not type 1. ST060 is the clean type 1 case.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
