timestamp=2026-11-09T08:16:21.295Z level=INFO run=5a234059 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# ST023’s residuals have stronger correlation with rain. Also its aggregate is very close to peers. This fits type 3 better.\n# So the three likely are: ST060 (type 1, rhythm/phase), ST066 (type 2, muted), ST023 (type 3, rain-correlated residuals).\n# Let us confirm all are different and make sense. Type 1 is in PM10 only? ST060 is PM10 station. Type 2 and 3 are PM25. That’s fine as long as they exhibit the described behaviors. The dataset has both pollutants; faulty behavior can manifest in the data they report.\n# Also check if there are other obvious extreme outliers like ST040 — but the question says 3 stations with different types. ST040 is probably not among these 3; it’s more blatantly broken. The three described are more subtle.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
